<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ukit Kan Le'k Tok'</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 801</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ukit Kan Le'k Tok' was a Maya king of Ek' Balam in north-eastern Yucatán who took power in 770 and made the city the capital of a regional kingdom, Talol. He died around 801 and was buried in the great Acropolis, in a tomb behind a stucco facade shaped as the jaws of a monster and decorated with winged figures, among the best-preserved Maya stucco work.</p></div>
